  "notes": "Drawn from 2024-2026 photos of the A320neo/A321neo and A350 in the 2023 scheme. The fin layout is the same on both sides relative to the direction of flight. Widebodies (A350, 787, 777) carry red/purple/gold art on the winglets/raked tips; the A320 family has plain gold sharklets. Exact brand hexes not published in a source found; colors matched by eye. Many older aircraft still wear the 2007 scheme (standard-2007), and ex-Vistara A320neo/A321neo/787-9 aircraft fly in Vistara's aubergine scheme with 'Operated by Air India' titles until repainted. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on VT-RTN (flipped, fitted to the measured A320 shape): the title runs x 0.162 to 0.477, its baseline about 0.84 m under the windows' middle and its capitals' tops 0.89 m over it (y -0.05 to 0.54, placed by the windows: the fit tilts a little along the fuselage); it had been drawn about 0.27 m taller. The belly fairing's red and its gold outline are curves (smooth); their places agree with the photo within the fit's error.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Introduced 2023-08 (unveiled 2023-08-10; first A350 delivered in it 2024-01), replacing the 2007 red-swan / Konark-wheel scheme, which still flies on part of the fleet (standard-2007)."
